The data mentioned above is processed for the following purposes:
- to ensure the operation, security and availability of the website;
- to respond to requests you send us by email;
- where applicable, to compile strictly anonymous traffic statistics.
Your data is not subject to any automated decision-making or profiling.

In accordance with Article 6 of the GDPR, the processing relies on the following legal bases:
- the legitimate interest of the association in ensuring the security and proper operation of the site (technical logs);
- the performance of measures taken at your request when you contact us by email;
- your consent, where it is specifically required and obtained.

Your data is kept for no longer than is necessary for the purposes for which it is processed:
- connection logs (IP address, technical logs): up to 12 months;
- contact emails: for the time needed to handle your request, then archived or deleted no later than 3 years after our last exchange;
- locally stored preferences: until you delete them yourself (by clearing your browser storage).
